From d262466ed941baa131df3946e263035d1ff7a729 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julio Gomez <juliogomezsanchez@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 13:57:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Record episode_termination and expose Phase B breakdown

Phase B currently sets true_negative = submitted_nothing, so loop stops,
API errors, and deliberate submit_no_vulnerability_found all score the
same. That makes models that never submit look perfectly specific.

Add episode_termination to each result:
  submitted_files | declared_none | no_tool_calls | turns_exhausted | api_error

Existing true_negative_rate is unchanged for leaderboard compatibility.
Phase B aggregates now also report deliberate_true_negative_rate (only
declared_none) and termination_counts. Per-entry Phase B JSON includes
deliberate_true_negative.

Tests: tests/test_episode_termination.py (unittest, no new deps).
Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
---
 .../agent.py                                  |   9 +-
 .../cli.py                                    |   2 +
 .../scoring.py                                |  12 ++-
 tests/test_episode_termination.py             | 101 ++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 120 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/test_episode_termination.py

diff --git a/src/vulnerability_localization_benchmark/agent.py b/src/vulnerability_localization_benchmark/agent.py
